WEBVTT

00:21.896 --> 00:23.773
The patrol aircraft went to confirm

00:24.399 --> 00:27.152
that they couldn't escape.

00:29.112 --> 00:33.158
We could just corner
the enemy scientist and kill him.

00:34.200 --> 00:36.411
Kill him?

00:36.995 --> 00:39.622
According to this guy over here, Mr. Gen,

00:39.706 --> 00:41.958
they have a single genius scientist.

00:42.542 --> 00:44.127
If that's the case,

00:44.210 --> 00:47.464
we just need to get rid of that leader

00:48.506 --> 00:52.093
to destroy the Little Kingdom of Science.

00:55.555 --> 00:57.682
<i>That Dr. Taiju.</i>

01:00.143 --> 01:02.812
That's smart, for real…

01:02.896 --> 01:05.607
But can you do that?

01:11.905 --> 01:13.114
Of course.

01:16.201 --> 01:17.702
How?

01:19.454 --> 01:21.539
We simply can.

01:22.540 --> 01:26.628
Oh, Mr. Gen. If Stan says he can,

01:26.711 --> 01:29.631
there's no need to ask any further.

01:31.382 --> 01:33.551
He can do it.

01:34.260 --> 01:37.138
<i>I'm so sorry, dear Dr. Taiju…</i>

01:37.222 --> 01:40.809
<i>I need to warn him that I sent</i>
<i>some skilled assassins after him,</i>

01:40.892 --> 01:43.019
<i>and that he should be careful, but…</i>

01:43.645 --> 01:46.231
<i>our radio communications</i>
<i>can be intercepted,</i>

01:46.981 --> 01:50.401
<i>and they're keeping a close eye on me,</i>
<i>so I can't contact them.</i>

01:58.034 --> 02:01.287
<i>This is bad…</i>

02:01.996 --> 02:07.460
&lrm;ORIGINAL WORK: RIICHIRO INAGAKI, BOICHI
&lrm;SHUEISHA JUMP COMICS

03:49.520 --> 03:53.358
Can we actually trust that Gen?

03:54.150 --> 03:55.735
Trust?

03:55.818 --> 04:00.281
If anyone would trust an enemy
who turned his back on his own so quickly,

04:00.365 --> 04:03.743
they should see a psychiatrist.

04:04.994 --> 04:08.957
We'll keep him alive somehow
until we get some information from him.

04:09.040 --> 04:11.417
He's probably a spy, anyway…

04:12.627 --> 04:15.588
Yes, of course!

04:15.672 --> 04:17.632
I knew it, too.

04:17.715 --> 04:23.972
I was just testing you to see if you would
ever let your guard down, Stanley.

04:31.479 --> 04:33.690
Why did you stop, Luna?

04:33.773 --> 04:36.442
No… Aren't you the one who is too fast?

04:39.279 --> 04:41.114
Look, my lady!

04:41.197 --> 04:42.949
I'm carrying five bottles of water!

04:43.032 --> 04:44.200
That's a lot!

04:44.284 --> 04:46.744
You sure talk big! Don't you know

04:46.828 --> 04:50.206
I deliberately shorted
the amount of water I put in?

04:50.290 --> 04:53.584
Carlos! Max! You are too slow!

04:53.668 --> 04:55.878
You're only carrying water and food!

04:55.962 --> 04:57.505
Still, isn't it too much?

04:57.588 --> 04:59.632
Why this amount?

04:59.716 --> 05:02.885
See? I'm not complaining, my lady!

05:02.969 --> 05:06.472
I'm different from this fake picker-upper!

05:06.556 --> 05:09.517
Your legs are like a newborn fawn’s.

05:10.643 --> 05:11.853
Stop it!

05:17.358 --> 05:18.901
They're so useless…

05:20.320 --> 05:23.323
But it can't be helped, anyway!

05:23.406 --> 05:25.241
Let me carry some of it, too.

05:25.325 --> 05:29.329
No way, my lady! I'll handle all of it!

05:29.412 --> 05:31.039
What are you trying to show off?

05:31.122 --> 05:33.875
Stay back, I'll carry it!

05:36.627 --> 05:39.505
It can't be helped…

05:39.589 --> 05:41.799
Luna, do not carry it yourself.

05:41.883 --> 05:43.885
But, those two…

05:49.015 --> 05:51.017
Don't get me wrong.

05:51.100 --> 05:54.103
I'm not saying you don't need to carry it,
I'm saying don't carry it.

05:55.980 --> 05:59.400
Don't let carrying heavy luggage
leave marks on your body.

05:59.901 --> 06:02.987
You've got work to do after this.

06:05.573 --> 06:07.283
Work?

06:19.629 --> 06:21.339
<i>The air feels stagnant.</i>

06:22.548 --> 06:23.591
<i>&lrm;That's a bad omen.</i>

06:24.675 --> 06:27.595
<i>My sailor's intuition never fails…</i>

06:31.432 --> 06:33.476
Is that the enemy ship?

06:33.559 --> 06:36.395
It's huge!

06:38.523 --> 06:40.942
Isn't the enemy scientist skilled as well?

06:41.025 --> 06:43.277
They can't beat Xeno, though…

06:45.822 --> 06:49.033
Are those the ones that measure
temperature and humidity?

06:50.785 --> 06:52.787
Is that a weathervane?

06:52.870 --> 06:56.415
It's our caring housewife Dr. Xeno's work.

06:56.499 --> 06:59.877
He said it was fine as long as
we understood everything by instinct.

06:59.961 --> 07:03.047
The more data, the more accurate.

07:04.382 --> 07:06.843
What is he researching?

07:06.926 --> 07:09.095
Is it weather information?

07:10.805 --> 07:13.099
It affects the speed of bullets.

07:24.735 --> 07:27.780
Are you serious? From this far?

07:29.699 --> 07:31.659
I'll snipe him down.

07:34.495 --> 07:36.998
Snipe?

07:38.541 --> 07:40.960
The enemy scientist leader.

07:41.043 --> 07:43.629
With Xeno's sniper rifle.

07:44.255 --> 07:46.883
-Sniper?
-That's right.

07:47.592 --> 07:49.427
We'll avoid an all-out conflict

07:49.510 --> 07:52.346
and quickly eliminate our key target.

07:52.430 --> 07:56.517
We'll resolve the battle
with minimal damage.

07:56.601 --> 08:01.355
Don't you think the sniper adds an element
of elegance and science to the battle?

08:10.156 --> 08:12.783
<i>We already did the reconnaisance</i>
<i>with the patrol aircraft.</i>

08:12.867 --> 08:14.535
<i>This is the best position.</i>

08:15.119 --> 08:17.038
Are we killing…

08:17.705 --> 08:20.458
Only their scientific leader.

08:20.541 --> 08:23.336
Sure, but isn't that a bit pitiful?

08:30.426 --> 08:31.969
In this manner,

08:32.053 --> 08:34.847
it is my job to be sure
that those two softies

08:34.931 --> 08:37.475
don't give in to cowardice.

08:37.558 --> 08:39.268
My lady is so cool!

08:39.352 --> 08:41.437
It's mesmerizing!

08:42.063 --> 08:45.733
By the way, what did you mean
when you said I had work to do?

08:45.816 --> 08:48.653
What are these striped clothes for?

08:49.237 --> 08:51.531
They're awesome, you look really cute.

08:51.614 --> 08:54.450
Stanley is a man too,
he's interested in the ladys' charms,

08:54.534 --> 08:55.910
isn't he?

08:56.494 --> 08:58.579
One stripe is five inches.

08:59.121 --> 09:00.289
It's a scale.

09:01.040 --> 09:04.335
With a few adjustments,
I can tell the distance to the target.

09:06.671 --> 09:09.090
<i>Since you're the same age as them, Luna,</i>

09:09.173 --> 09:11.968
<i>you're the most likely to go unnoticed.</i>

09:12.051 --> 09:17.056
<i>You'll sneak in the ship</i>
<i>and find the scientific leader, Dr. Taiju.</i>

09:17.640 --> 09:18.849
<i>Three seconds will be enough.</i>

09:18.933 --> 09:20.685
<i>&lrm;Just lead him out onto the deck</i>
<i>&lrm;for three seconds,</i>

09:20.768 --> 09:22.937
<i>and signal that it's him.</i>

09:24.105 --> 09:25.898
<i>I'll finish him in one shot.</i>

09:34.740 --> 09:37.660
<i>I'm Luna, the cool girl.</i>

09:37.743 --> 09:40.538
<i>I'm Luna, the all-mighty girl!</i>

09:45.543 --> 09:48.462
<i>They could save themselves</i>
<i>if they fled to the ocean,</i>

09:48.546 --> 09:49.922
<i>&lrm;but they won't move.</i>

09:50.840 --> 09:53.426
<i>They won't abandon their friend.</i>

09:53.509 --> 09:56.304
<i>It's the sweetness you often see in kids…</i>

10:00.558 --> 10:02.476
<i>They're of that kind…</i>

10:03.185 --> 10:07.732
-Help! Help me!
<i>-They won't ignore a woman in need.</i>

10:10.234 --> 10:14.030
<i>If they're sending in spies,</i>
<i>we'll have to counterattack.</i>

10:14.989 --> 10:18.075
<i>We'll pay them back.</i>

10:18.909 --> 10:20.536
What happened? Are you okay?

10:20.620 --> 10:22.079
Help me, please!

10:22.747 --> 10:26.542
I'm desperately escaping
from Dr. Xeno's dreadful kingdom…

10:27.335 --> 10:28.252
Dr. Xeno?

10:29.420 --> 10:30.504
She's cute!

10:30.588 --> 10:33.007
I don't think
this is a good time for that.

10:34.884 --> 10:36.510
<i>This is a tough decision.</i>

10:37.553 --> 10:39.930
<i>I would like to help her,</i>

10:40.014 --> 10:42.016
<i>but we can't just take it at face value.</i>

10:42.683 --> 10:44.685
<i>What shall we do, Senku?</i>

10:47.396 --> 10:48.856
Are you okay?

10:48.939 --> 10:52.652
You're safe now. Come on board.

10:56.489 --> 10:57.823
Thank you…

11:00.368 --> 11:03.454
Let's treat her injuries in the back!

11:06.874 --> 11:09.960
-Senku's making…
-Such a pretty face.

11:19.637 --> 11:22.181
Infiltration accomplished!
That's our lady!

11:22.264 --> 11:24.558
The enemy fell for her, too!

11:24.642 --> 11:30.356
Damn Stanley! He made my lady
cross such a dangerous bridge.

11:31.107 --> 11:36.195
But, how long is he going to
have to wait to snipe him down…

11:37.905 --> 11:41.826
I see, until my lady
lures the target onto the deck,

11:41.909 --> 11:44.662
whenever that may be…

11:44.745 --> 11:47.248
So, with all this water,

11:47.331 --> 11:50.751
he can focus and wait
for hundreds of hours.

11:50.835 --> 11:54.547
Stanley is kind of a monster…

11:54.630 --> 11:59.176
So, which one of them
is the so-called young genius,

11:59.260 --> 12:01.262
Dr. Taiju…

12:06.600 --> 12:10.271
Hey! let me treat your wounds, over here.

12:10.354 --> 12:11.939
&lrm;She seems suspicious.

12:12.022 --> 12:14.692
Is it really okay
that we let her board our ship?

12:14.775 --> 12:16.944
It's fine!
She's got a pretty face, after all.

12:18.279 --> 12:21.740
Well, Senku is a man too!
She probably hit a soft spot!

12:21.824 --> 12:24.577
Her blonde hair is striking too, isn't it?

12:24.660 --> 12:27.455
That sounds wrong, no matter what.

12:31.083 --> 12:32.126
That woman…

12:32.877 --> 12:34.753
There's a 50 percent chance…

12:34.837 --> 12:37.298
No, there's a 70 percent chance
that she's a spy like Gen.

12:38.883 --> 12:40.384
That's okay.

12:40.468 --> 12:44.013
We're going to get plenty of info
about Xeno from that woman.

12:45.181 --> 12:49.310
We'll send an encrypted message
to Tukasa's Special Forces unit.

12:49.393 --> 12:52.813
Information is science's
most powerful weapon.

12:52.897 --> 12:54.690
Spy versus spy.

12:54.773 --> 12:57.818
A battle of wits between tricksters.

12:57.902 --> 13:00.362
So that's what it is!

13:17.421 --> 13:20.341
I don't see anything
that looks like the enemy base.

13:20.966 --> 13:22.843
We only know roughly

13:22.927 --> 13:25.304
where Chrome's group might be.

13:25.387 --> 13:27.223
I wish we knew a bit more.

13:29.558 --> 13:33.395
I want to take the upper hand
by taking the enemy scientific leader.

13:36.482 --> 13:39.527
If we could get enemy intel
just a bit sooner than they do…

13:41.237 --> 13:43.614
Yes! I was thinking

13:43.697 --> 13:47.868
that we could cooperate
in order to revive all of humanity.

13:48.452 --> 13:50.746
We cannot surrender and serve you,

13:50.829 --> 13:53.457
but we are available to negotiate anytime!

13:55.543 --> 13:57.670
So, the enemy can hear this too?

13:57.753 --> 13:59.296
It's a radio broadcast.

13:59.380 --> 14:02.466
We at least have to try.

14:04.218 --> 14:07.388
<i>We have no idea</i>
<i>what kind of person Dr. Xeno is.</i>

14:21.068 --> 14:23.362
<i>My mission</i>

14:24.446 --> 14:28.784
<i>is to find the scientific leader,</i>
<i>Dr. Taiju, and lead him onto the deck…</i>

14:29.785 --> 14:32.663
<i>This is a tough one.</i>
<i>There are too many of them!</i>

14:35.040 --> 14:36.125
<i>It's okay!</i>

14:36.208 --> 14:38.669
<i>Because I'm Luna, the cool woman!</i>

14:38.752 --> 14:40.170
<i>Luna, the all-mighty woman!</i>

14:40.838 --> 14:42.464
<i>Who could Dr. Taiju be?</i>

14:42.548 --> 14:44.925
<i>I can't just go and ask.</i>

14:45.009 --> 14:47.636
<i>They're still watching me closely.</i>

14:49.054 --> 14:51.181
<i>If my analysis is correct…</i>

14:52.099 --> 14:54.935
<i>The intellect of a single person</i>
<i>brought these kids</i>

14:55.019 --> 14:58.564
<i>from the stone age</i>
<i>to this level of scientific progress.</i>

14:58.647 --> 15:03.110
<i>He must be a very intelligent person</i>
<i>with a strong conviction.</i>

15:03.777 --> 15:06.280
<i>That is totally my type!</i>

15:06.864 --> 15:10.701
<i>In other words, I just have to</i>
<i>look for someone who is my type.</i>

15:11.535 --> 15:15.915
<i>I guess, a mission where a woman</i>
<i>just has to follow her own feelings</i>

15:15.998 --> 15:18.918
<i>will be easy to accomplish.</i>

15:22.838 --> 15:24.214
<i>What about this man?</i>

15:25.424 --> 15:27.051
<i>No.</i>

15:30.930 --> 15:32.139
<i>What about this one?</i>

15:36.143 --> 15:37.311
<i>No.</i>

15:38.520 --> 15:39.855
<i>This one?</i>

15:41.023 --> 15:41.857
<i>&lrm;No.</i>

15:45.569 --> 15:47.571
<i>Definitely not him!</i>

15:52.201 --> 15:54.203
<i>There's also a chance</i>
<i>he won't show up easily</i>

15:54.286 --> 15:57.122
<i>in front of an outsider like me.</i>

15:57.206 --> 16:00.250
<i>I have to be prepared for a final showdown</i>

16:00.334 --> 16:02.252
<i>with Dr. Taiju himself.</i>

16:04.088 --> 16:06.048
-Ah, Taiju!
-Yes?

16:09.593 --> 16:11.303
We were looking for you.

16:11.387 --> 16:13.973
There's some stuff
too heavy for us to carry.

16:14.056 --> 16:16.517
Sorry about that.
I'll get back to it right now!

16:23.691 --> 16:26.235
<i>I had some preconceived ideas</i>
<i>about scientists,</i>

16:26.318 --> 16:27.611
<i>but it's okay.</i>

16:27.695 --> 16:31.699
<i>If it were anyone else,</i>
<i>they might have missed you, Dr. Taiju.</i>

16:31.782 --> 16:34.368
<i>That was tough!</i>

16:34.451 --> 16:37.371
<i>He might be</i>
<i>a dedicated scientist on this ship</i>

16:37.454 --> 16:39.540
<i>and just doesn't show it easily.</i>

16:39.623 --> 16:42.376
<i>How could I get him onto the deck?</i>

16:43.293 --> 16:47.214
I'll go right away onto the deck!

16:50.050 --> 16:51.844
<i>I just have to point him out!</i>

16:54.430 --> 16:55.597
<i>Then…</i>

16:56.181 --> 16:59.309
Hey! You said you were Luna, right?

17:00.477 --> 17:02.104
I'm Senku.

17:02.604 --> 17:05.774
<i>The pretty Senku feels really off.</i>

17:05.858 --> 17:10.029
<i>He's trying to extract information</i>
<i>about Dr. Xeno carefully.</i>

17:10.988 --> 17:14.033
I need information about Xeno.
Tell me everything.

17:17.411 --> 17:18.787
-Senku!
-Yes?

17:19.621 --> 17:22.958
What is it?
I'm in the middle of an interrogation.

17:23.042 --> 17:25.586
Francois wants to extend
his hospitality to our guest.

17:26.336 --> 17:29.840
We would appreciate it
if you would open up to us.

17:30.466 --> 17:32.843
You may use our Bar Francois
as much as you like.

17:37.765 --> 17:40.601
Persuasion is about fulfilling desires.

17:41.477 --> 17:43.896
Since I do not know Luna's tastes,

17:43.979 --> 17:46.065
I can only guess what she might like.

17:46.857 --> 17:51.111
In that case, how about that food
that everyone around the world loves?

17:51.195 --> 17:52.112
That is…

17:53.697 --> 17:55.115
ice cream!

17:55.199 --> 17:57.409
Where do you get your data?

17:57.493 --> 17:59.620
I'm an expert in what people want,
I've done my research.

18:00.287 --> 18:05.000
But honestly, I can't think of any
other food that fewer people dislike.

18:05.084 --> 18:08.629
I've pretty much never heard
of anyone who doesn't like it.

18:09.338 --> 18:11.256
The ingredients are quite simple.

18:12.091 --> 18:16.178
I'll use milk, sugar,
and some powdered kudzu

18:16.261 --> 18:19.348
made from ground kudzu root
instead of gelatin.

18:19.431 --> 18:21.266
It has a smooth texture.

18:21.850 --> 18:24.311
I'd need vanilla extract too…

18:28.107 --> 18:32.069
Vanilla doesn't grow in America either,
so we'll have to produce it with science.

18:32.152 --> 18:36.532
Ah, I remember you did something
similar on Valentine's Day.

18:37.241 --> 18:39.326
I'll wrap a copper wire
around a test tube,

18:40.035 --> 18:42.037
put a bit of iron inside,

18:42.121 --> 18:45.749
and switch on the high-voltage!

18:47.042 --> 18:49.044
It's flickering purple!

18:52.798 --> 18:55.050
What are they doing?

18:58.137 --> 19:01.557
-It stinks like a pool!
-It’s more like photocopier smell.

19:01.640 --> 19:03.392
It's producing ozone.

19:04.184 --> 19:07.563
This is getting further and further
from ice cream, is that okay?

19:07.646 --> 19:08.772
Will we get back to it?

19:10.149 --> 19:13.026
When simmering bay laurel extract

19:13.110 --> 19:16.113
with our familiar sodium hydroxide,

19:16.196 --> 19:18.574
and bubble it with the ozone,

19:19.825 --> 19:22.369
we get vanilla extract!

19:22.953 --> 19:26.748
-Suddenly…
-There's a sweet aroma.

19:30.794 --> 19:34.381
I'll mix the ingredients I prepared
earlier while cooling them down.

19:34.464 --> 19:36.341
If you add salt to ice

19:36.425 --> 19:38.635
it will lower the temperature
by ten degrees.

19:45.350 --> 19:47.102
<i>Dr. Taiju is on the deck again!</i>

19:47.186 --> 19:49.146
<i>If I get next to him and point him out…</i>

19:51.815 --> 19:55.903
What are you doing?
You should be resting if you're hurt.

19:57.237 --> 20:00.240
Thanks, it's okay…

20:00.324 --> 20:02.743
Finally, we'll place it in a bag

20:03.327 --> 20:04.912
and squeeze it out.

20:07.706 --> 20:10.751
Our soft-serve is complete.

20:16.381 --> 20:17.382
Here.

20:52.459 --> 20:54.461
With that electricity from before…

20:55.170 --> 20:58.465
How did he… Was there vanilla?

20:58.548 --> 21:01.468
If there wasn't any,
we'll just do something about it.

21:02.010 --> 21:04.471
That's what humanity has been doing
for two million years.

21:05.389 --> 21:09.476
That's the very source of this world.
We reached down to the molecular level

21:09.559 --> 21:12.437
and created things
that were not supposed to exist.

21:12.521 --> 21:14.481
That's the thrill of organic chemistry.

21:17.818 --> 21:19.528
<i>No, wait!</i>

21:19.611 --> 21:21.989
<i>I'm into intelligent people.</i>

21:22.072 --> 21:24.741
<i>That would be Dr. Taiju,</i>
<i>the scientific leader!</i>

21:24.825 --> 21:28.078
You're doing quite well, aren't you?

21:28.161 --> 21:30.289
As Xeno likes to say:

21:30.372 --> 21:33.000
"It's so…

21:35.210 --> 21:36.670
elegant!"

21:40.007 --> 21:41.258
Luna.

21:42.884 --> 21:45.804
Did Dr. Xeno use to be a NASA scientist?

21:46.805 --> 21:48.307
How would you know that?

21:53.645 --> 21:54.563
What is it?

21:58.150 --> 21:59.443
<i>Dr. Xeno was,</i>

22:00.360 --> 22:02.571
<i>from the very beginning, my mentor…</i>

22:09.536 --> 22:12.414
…in the science of rocket-making.

23:53.098 --> 23:55.892
NEXT EPISODE

23:55.976 --> 23:56.935
THIS WORK OF FICTION FEATURES ORGANISMS,
MATERIAL AND PROCESSES BASED ON REAL LIFE.

23:57.018 --> 23:58.228
COLLECTING OR REPLICATING THEM
MAY BE DANGEROUS AND ILLEGAL,

23:58.311 --> 23:59.271
SO DO NOT ATTEMPT.

23:59.354 --> 24:00.897
Subtitle translation by: Silvia
